1. Write a FAILING test in skill_wire.rs's #[cfg(test)] mod tests: run the Store step with an extracted Skill (build a fixture Skill), assert the skill is afterwards recalled via recall_skills/fts5 (reuse the existing store_skill_then_recall_finds_it_via_fts5 pattern).
2. Run it, confirm it fails.
3. Thread the extracted Skill into the Store dispatch (e.g. give run_skill_step(Store) access to the payload, or have the Store branch call store_skill(&skill)); keep skill_store() returning a typed error only when there is genuinely no payload.
4. Run `cargo test --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml skill_wire` — all green, no regressions.
REPORT what you changed + the test result. Touch only skill_wire.rs (+ a fixture). Do NOT add dependencies. Do NOT run cargo fmt repo-wide.
